# WCAG 2.2 AA And Mobile View For Web Pages

## Target

User-visible surfaces (React SPA under `/machine/` including `/machine/api-key`, and operator templates) must **maintain alignment with WCAG 2.2 Level AA** and **remain usable on mobile viewports** whenever those pages or their shared styles are changed.

Documented limitations (e.g. Bokeh canvas for screen readers, OAuth IdP UI) do not relax requirements for everything the app controls.

## WCAG 2.2 AA (when touching web UI)

- **Keyboard**: All interactive controls reachable and operable without a pointer; predictable focus order; **Escape** (and Tab traps where modals exist) behave correctly; visible **`:focus-visible`** (do not remove outlines without an equivalent).
- **Semantics**: Correct landmarks (`main`, `nav`, labeled regions/dialogs), headings in logical order, **labels** / **`aria-*`** on forms and dynamic status (e.g. `aria-live` where appropriate), tables with **`scope`** / captions when tabular.
- **Perceivable**: Sufficient **contrast** for text and UI chrome; do not rely on **color alone** for meaning; respect **`prefers-reduced-motion`** for non-essential animation.
- **Titles**: Keep **`useDocumentTitle`** (or equivalent) accurate for the view after your change.
- **Verification**: Run frontend tests (`npm test -- --run` under `hpcperfstats/site/frontend`). Follow **Accessibility** in [`docs/TESTING.md`](docs/TESTING.md) for manual checks on substantive UX changes.

## Bokeh plots (app-controlled mitigation)

- **Never** place `BokehEmbed` inside `<button>` or another interactive control (use a separate enlarge/open control).
- Every user-facing `BokehEmbed` must expose limitation prose via `aria-describedby` (canonical: [`BokehPlotWithLimitation.jsx`](hpcperfstats/site/frontend/src/components/BokehPlotWithLimitation.jsx) or Job Detail `PlotPanel`).

## Custom dialogs and overlays

- Match Extended Search in [`Layout.jsx`](hpcperfstats/site/frontend/src/Layout.jsx): `role="dialog"`, `aria-modal="true"`, `aria-labelledby`, backdrop or `inert` on page content behind, `useFocusTrap`, Escape closes, restore focus to activator.
- Initial focus: title or primary field — not dismiss-only control.

## Forms, tables, and color

- If a field sets `aria-invalid` or `aria-describedby`, referenced ids **must exist** in the DOM (pair error props with visible or `invalid-feedback` nodes).
- Data tables: `<caption>` (visually-hidden OK) and `scope` on `<th>`; single-column lists need a header or caption.
- Do not rely on **color alone** (row `backgroundColor`, badges without text, etc.); provide a non-visual equivalent.

## Mobile view (when touching any webpage)

Any edit to a **page, route-level layout, or component that affects layout** must **preserve or improve small-screen behavior**:

- Use existing breakpoints and patterns in `hpcperfstats/site/frontend/src/index.css` (e.g. `max-width: 991.98px` / `767.98px`) or Bootstrap responsive utilities; add or adjust rules when the desktop layout would break stacking, overflow, or touch targets on narrow widths.
- Aim for **minimum ~44×44 CSS px** touch targets for primary controls where feasible (pagination, toggles, primary buttons); avoid horizontal-only critical flows without a scroll container.
- After layout or chrome changes, **mentally verify** (or briefly test) **~375px width**: navbar, tables in `.table-responsive`, plot areas, dialogs, and forms.

## Overlap

- Complements **`react-js-cursor-rule.mdc`** (component style and tests on touch).
- Complements **`web-pages-e2e-test-maintenance.mdc`** when routes or visible behavior changes.
- Complements **`no-scientific-notation-web.mdc`** for numeric display; accessibility rules do not override it.
- Complements **`frontend-a11y-regression.mdc`** for jest-axe / Playwright smoke requirements.
- Django **admin** HTML: keep keyboard behavior and upstream admin patterns intact; add minimal chrome (e.g. back link) without breaking admin templates.
